{
  "id": "PE01Z",
  "version": "2.0",
  "title": "Pulmonary function testing",
  "description": "Pulmonary function testing measures how well your lungs work, including how much air they hold and how quickly you can move air in and out. These breathing tests help diagnose and monitor conditions such as asthma, chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD), and other lung problems. During the test, you breathe into a mouthpiece connected to a machine and follow simple coaching, such as taking a deep breath and blowing out as hard and fast as you can. Some tests measure your lung volumes, check how your airways respond to a medication, or track your breathing during light exercise. The tests are painless and non-invasive, take about 30 to 90 minutes depending on how many are done, and give your doctor a clear picture of your lung health.",
